      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As a reference, I have to constantly deal with my camera being at the floor, while my cross-legged animation results in my avatar head being where the lower torso would be, making my camera being located at the legs rather than the head, making for misalignment from where my head looks to where I'm looking.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-11-14T16:38:29.926Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The ability to use a slider to modify the height margins which shift between standing, crouching, and crawling animations for 3-Point or 4-Point Tracking VR users.\nCertain VR headsets that have their cameras mounted to the headset such as the WMR do not track height well from what VRChat considers the height from ground for crawling. \nThis feature would certainly aid for users who use custom crawling animations such as cross-legged animations, as the position would be at the head, rather than at where the legs would be as it currently is now.\n[Could also be titled: Head position does not match position of avatar head for custom crawling animation when in VR]",
